      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, hold on. You said the control group is showing a statistically significant upward trend with a p-value of less than 0.01? \n\nIf the control group is improving that much, that would actually make it much harder to prove the drug is working. That doesn't sound like a \"clean\" result for us. Can you double-check those specific control group scores? I need to know if those improvements are actual data or if there's a mistake in how the variance is being calculated.",
